#
# Cache rules.
#
# Rule numbering follows the dispatcher convention: later rules win, so the defaults come
# first and each AeroVance exception below narrows them.
#

$include "./default_rules.any"

#
# AeroVance cache exceptions.
#
# Everything here is a decision about what is safe to hand to a second visitor. The default
# is to cache, and each rule below names something whose response belongs to one person, or
# changes faster than a page invalidation would notice.
#

# The stock ticker fragment, fetched by the dispatcher through Sling Dynamic Include.
# Excluded from the page cache because it carries its own short TTL: a share price and a
# page about company history have nothing in common in how often they change, and caching
# them together would force the whole investor-relations section to expire every fifteen
# minutes. The matching SDI configuration lives in ui.config.
/0100 { /type "deny" /glob "/content/mysite/*.nocache.html*" }

# Careers results. The page renders whatever the applicant tracking system says right now,
# and a requisition that closes must stop being advertised within minutes rather than at the
# next content activation — which for a careers page may be weeks away. Caching is left to
# the service's own short-lived in-memory cache, which at least bounds the call volume.
/0101 { /type "deny" /glob "/content/mysite/*/careers*" }

# Gated downloads. The response is one visitor's document, served after their lead form was
# accepted; the servlet also sends Cache-Control: private, no-store. Both belt and braces are
# deliberate — a gated whitepaper served from cache to the next visitor defeats the entire
# gate, and silently.
/0102 { /type "deny" /glob "*.download.html*" }

# The gated asset tree itself is denied to everyone on publish (see the repoinit script in
# ui.config), so a direct request 404s. This rule means the dispatcher does not cache that
# 404 either, which would otherwise persist after an ACL correction.
/0103 { /type "deny" /glob "/content/dam/mysite/gated/*" }
